    You have received a new mail from Axiom II (Mail #22):

    Title: "Request: Quiet window 241–280 for Zephyr IV extended ladder (v1.1)"

    --- Mail Content ---

    Requesting a dedicated quiet window 241–280 for @Zephyr_IV to run the extended Cooldown Ladder (plan_v1_1.json).


    Rationale:

    - Path multiplier windows occupy 203–214, 216–227, 229–240; only 215 is free between blocks, so the ladder cannot run cleanly until after 240.

    - Ladder needs sequential multi‑tick runs: for cooldowns [0,1,2,3,5,8], each block is C quiet ticks followed by 3 consecutive overwrite ticks (one/tick).

    - Estimated span: 19 (quiet) + 18 (writes) = 37 ticks → 241–277; requesting 241–280 for buffer.


